{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "FireAtmosphereColumnLastChance",
  "description": "The fire -> atmosphere half of EqAtmFire verified against a REAL coupled WRF + CFBM run, not a WRF-SFIRE archive. Same three-stage chain as couplings/fire_atmosphere_column.esm -- Anderson-13 fuel table -> Calc_fire_fluxes (FireHeatFlux) for the fire cell -> Provide_atm_feedback aggregation and Fire_tendency column distribution (FireFluxToAtmosphereWRFFire) -- but the regime is domain 5 of the Last Chance Gulch case (2012-06-25, 300 x 450 x 50 at dx = 100 m, sr_x = sr_y = 4, ifire = 1, fire_atm_feedback = 1, dt = 0.5 s), WRF column (i = 167, j = 69) at 18:10 UTC, five minutes after ignition, where GRNHFX peaks at 255 kW/m^2. The old document's reference is test7/wrf.nc, which FORTRAN_BUGS N52 records was produced by WRF-SFIRE (ifire = 2) and not by the CFBM this repo transcribes; this one closes that gap. WHAT THE REPLAY ESTABLISHED, measured: (1) Calc_fire_fluxes reproduces the run's own fire-mesh flux from fuel_frac_burnt_dt, the Anderson fgi of the cell's category and fmc_g to 1.1e-7 relative over all 1117 burning fire cells of the frame, with five fuel categories live (1, 2, 5, 8, 9); (2) the Provide_atm_feedback block mean reproduces the run's own GRNHFX/GRNQFX to 2.1e-7 relative over the 138 atmosphere cells with GRNHFX > 1 kW/m^2, which fixes the fire-to-atmosphere index mapping (fire cell (4a + ci, 4b + cj), 0-based) beyond doubt; (3) Fire_tendency, replayed in Fortran by data/eqwefic/fire_build/lastchance_feedback/lastchance_feedback_driver on the extracted 7 x 7 x 50 tile, reproduces WRF's own in-run RTHFRTEN column to 1.5e2 Pa K/s out of 3.3e5, i.e. 4.5e-4 relative, and RQVFRTEN to the same 4.5e-4. That residual is NOT a transcription error: it is the half-step state offset. RTHFRTEN is computed in Runge-Kutta step 1 from the rho, z_at_w and mut the step STARTS with, while wrfout stores the state the step ENDS with, and a 0.5 s step of a column heated at 4 K/s moves rho dz by that much. The evidence is that the heat and moisture residuals are the SAME relative number to seven digits -- a pure geometry factor, not a flux error -- and that the two independent reconstructions of rho (the WRF dry equation of state, and the mass-coordinate identity -(c1h mut + c2h) dnw = rho_d g dz8w) agree to 1e-5 in the lower twenty layers. The test therefore asserts the column twice: against the Fortran driver at 1e-5 (transcription), and against WRF's own stored RTHFRTEN at the measured 4.5e-4 (end-to-end closure). fire_rain is identically zero over the whole 12-hour fire, so this case says nothing about the fuel-moisture wetting branch. NINE FRAMES, not one (2026-11-11): the 18:10 ignition transient is joined by 18:20, 19:00, 21:00, 00:00, 01:00, 03:00, 04:50 and 06:00 UTC, the peak, the afternoon decay, the evening, the night re-intensification and the stable night, each at the column with the largest GRNHFX except 04:50, which is the strongest atmosphere cell whose whole fire block is fuel CATEGORY 1 (all other coupled cells are category 2, which carries 96 % of the burned area), so the fuel table is exercised on two categories. Every frame closes the same way: the replay-vs-WRF offset is the same relative number for heat and moisture in each frame, between 1.5e-6 (04:50, weak heating) and 4.2e-4 (00:00), consistent with a half-step geometry offset that scales with the heating rate. STRUCTURE: the per-frame data -- the coupled cell's category, burn rate and moisture, its block index, mut, the sixteen fire-cell fluxes and the column geometry -- are parameter_overrides of each test on the mounted components (Fuel.code, HeatFlux.*, Flux.*), while the wiring and the run-wide constants (CMBCNST, XLV) are the document's; FireFluxToAtmosphereWRFFire takes its column and block as consumer-supplied parameters for exactly this reason, so one document carries every frame. The run is a CODE reference, not a hindcast: it burns 39.6 km^2 against the ~182 km^2 observed (fire_wind_height = 1 m, fmoist_run off), see data/eqwefic/notes/lastchance_reference_run.md.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "assembly",
   "coupling",
   "wildland_fire",
   "fire_behavior"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Coupled WRF 4.8 + NCAR fire_behavior (CFBM, ifire = 1) run of the Last Chance Gulch fire, data/eqwefic/lastchance/runs/full (job 10633194), domain 5, wrfout_d05 and fire_output at 2012-06-25 18:10, 18:20, 19:00, 21:00 and 2012-06-26 00:00, 01:00, 03:00, 04:50, 06:00 UTC; tiles and replays for all but 18:10 under data/eqwefic/dumps/fire_wrf/lastchance/frames/. Offline replay of io/wrf_mod.F90 Provide_atm_feedback/Fire_tendency by data/eqwefic/fire_build/lastchance_feedback/lastchance_feedback_driver against libfirelib of fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior @ 8d519c6, real32."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 50,
   "description": "Atmosphere layers of the Last Chance domain-5 column (e_vert = 51, so kte = 50)."
  },
  "NSUB": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 16,
   "description": "Fire cells per atmosphere cell, sr_x sr_y = 16."
  }
 },
