     "description": "Reference: the coupled Last Chance Gulch WRF + CFBM run at 2012-06-26 04:50 UTC (the one CATEGORY-1 (short grass) frame: the strongest burning atmosphere cell whose whole 4 x 4 fire block is category 1 at any of the 84 fire_output frames, chosen by argmax restricted to category-1 blocks so the fuel table is not exercised on category 2 alone (fgi = 0.166 kg/m^2 against category 2's 0.896)), domain 5, WRF column (i = 191, j = 68) 1-based, the column with the largest GRNHFX among all-category-1 blocks; fire cell (764, 270) 1-based, block index s = 8, nfuel_cat = 1, fuel_frac_burnt_dt = 0.00814175606 over dt = 0.5 s, fmc_g = 0.0799999982. Same two tiers as the 18:10 test. phi_h/phi_q are the run's own fire_output fgrnhfx/fgrnqfx of that cell; grnhfx/grnqfx and the two tendency columns are the offline Fortran replay (lastchance_feedback_driver, real32) on the 7 x 7 x 50 tile extracted from wrfout_d05 at that time: rel 1e-5 pointwise, Linf at 1e-5 of the column maximum. The SECOND pair of column assertions is the end-to-end closure against WRF's OWN stored RTHFRTEN/RQVFRTEN: measured max |replay - WRF| = 0.0147 Pa K/s (1.5e-06 of the column maximum 9667) and 5.4e-07 Pa/s, the same relative number in both, i.e. the half-step state offset of the 18:10 test, not a flux error; the tolerance is that measurement x 1.5 rounded up, recording what was measured rather than certifying agreement. Tile and replay: data/eqwefic/dumps/fire_wrf/lastchance/frames/0450_26/.",
